3. Contributions and permitted forks

The Author welcomes people who help improve the Software. The following is allowed and is not a violation of section 2:

(a) forking the repository on GitHub, as allowed by the GitHub Terms of Service, and modifying your fork to prepare bug reports, fixes, improvements and translations;
(b) submitting pull requests, issues, patches and translations to the official repository;
(c) using the build scripts and tests to verify your changes locally.

Rules for forks: a fork exists only to contribute back. Do not publish releases or installers from it, do not present it as an independent or official product, and keep this license and all notices in it. The Author may ask you to delete a fork that is used for other purposes.

Contribution license. By submitting a contribution you confirm that you wrote it or have the right to submit it, and you grant the Author a perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, non-exclusive, royalty-free, sublicensable license to use, copy, modify, translate, distribute and relicense the contribution as part of the Software and in any form. You keep the copyright in your contribution. The Author is not obliged to accept it and owes no payment for it. Contributors are credited in the repository history.

